ed from asylum  would you advocate a quota model  if criteria were put into place making  it possible to apply for asylum abroad  europe would most likely have to take in  hundreds of thousands every year  i believe we have to establish  transparent criteria  set conditions  and then a flexible quota really would  be the only approach  but i do think a quota would be the  right way forward  so you would combine refugee policy with  a targeted immigration policy  i want a refugee policy on the one hand  and a targeted immigration policy on the  other  beyond that it would be important and  sensible to conduct immigration policy  proactively for highly qualified  specialists  there are all kinds of possibilities  those are three models in all but  they're all needed  you've said that europe could use  skilled workers from africa that's  surely correct  but would also presuppose that language  courses are offered in these countries  of origin  not everyone speaks finnish estonian  german or czech  exactly  language is the key to integration  if we get the people if they come to us  they must be integrated integrate  themselves  and language really is the key to that  that's why i think it's good that the  city state of berlin my employer is now  going to offer language courses for  asylum applicants  tolerated refugees  we should expand that further because  most of these people really  fortress europe is an expression that  pretty much captures the european  union's asylum and refugee policy  the union always thought it's better to  solve the problems that make people want  to migrate in the first place  since the 1960s development aid policy  was always defined as an attempt to  fight the causes of poverty and other  reasons why people leave home  has this approach  where  and unfortunately  development cooperation will never  completely eliminate economic need  and armed conflict in developing  countries  however  without development cooperation the  influx would be far greater  some african development experts  criticize european and global  development aid by saying it would be  far better if african countries received  no aid  then they'd be forced to stand on their  own feet you believe that's a radical  and possibly misdirected idea  um  good development cooperation helps build  up democratic structures good governance  and helps educate people  for me all that legitimizes development  cooperation  and if there is no work the only chance  is to move elsewhere let's not call it  fleeing but immigration instead do you  think we have to look to the canadians  as a model and say we want targeted  immigration not refugee immigration do  we need the courage to say that's what  we're not that far apart from the  canadians  our immigration law has quite a lot of  opportunities for coming to germany  it's  we have openings for specialized workers  for professions with shortages  for caregivers for freelancers  those are liberal regulations not  restrictive ones  i don't think you can compare germany to  canada simply because the german  language isn't spoken globally  that still keeps  germany's labor minister sometimes says  based on her long time having lived in  the us that we need a welcoming culture  not just a new welcoming culture but one  for foreigners for immigrants for aliens  is that what we need  and not only on paper  a welcoming culture has to be lived it  has to be lived by people by  neighborhoods church congregations  muslim communities and sports clubs  thank you
 

